# ⭐ ONE deliberate exception, and it is not a secret: the stable key that signs cloud TEST builds.
# Without a committed key, each cloud build signs with a randomly generated one, Android refuses the
# install as an update, and every tester has to uninstall — which erases every home they have saved.
# This is a self-signed test certificate with the conventional debug password; it holds no account,
# no service and no store identity. The Play Store key is a different key, is never committed, and
# reaches the build as a secret. See the comment in app/build.gradle.kts.
!signing/vastufirst-debug.keystore

# Design bundle: keep the zip (source), ignore the extracted working copy (Impl PRD §0.1)
Design System/Final Designs/vastufirst-mobile-apps-implementation/

# Render harness (UI-POLISH §6): COMMIT the goldens (src/androidUnitTest/roborazzi/*.png), but
# never the transient verify diffs — they exist on disk for the CI artifact, not for the repo.
**/roborazzi/*_compare.png
**/roborazzi/*_actual.png

# Third-party floor plans used as private test input — never redistribute
Documents/Sample Floor plans/
tools/scan-eval/corpus/

# Python bytecode from the eval/gate scripts
scripts/__pycache__/
tools/scan-eval/__pycache__/
